{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be part of your care team. I understand you came in after having thoughts about driving into a tree. Can you tell me more about what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… I was driving and just felt this wave of sadness. I thought, ‘Just hit the tree and end it.’ But I didn’t do it. I told my psychiatrist this morning and she said to come here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you for sharing that. It takes courage. Are you having those thoughts now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not right now. I just feel numb. I’ve been through ECT before, but they’ve been tapering it down and I think that’s making things worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Given your history and recent thoughts, the psychiatry team wants to keep you here for monitoring while we arrange your next steps, including ECT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I guess I need it. My veins are really bad though—getting IVs is a nightmare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that. Because you’re going to need regular treatments, we’re planning to place a port-a-cath. It’s a small device under the skin that makes access easier and less painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Is that a surgery? Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a minor procedure, done with sedation. You’ll be comfortable. It usually takes about an hour. We’ll schedule it early next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds better than getting stuck every time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll also keep you on your current meds—gabapentin, omeprazole, tramadol, levothyroxine, and trazodone. Lithium was in your list, but your level this morning was low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking it, but maybe it’s not enough. My mood’s been slipping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The psychiatry team is starting you on 150 mg at night. We’ll check levels and may increase it. It can help stabilize your mood over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-09-04 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it. I just want to feel stable again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs came back—everything looks stable. Blood count, kidneys, thyroid—all normal. Your urine test showed methadone, but you’re not on it, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I haven’t taken methadone. Maybe it’s a false positive? I only take my prescribed meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll note that. No concerns otherwise. How’s your abdominal pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but it’s chronic. I think it’s from endometriosis. Tramadol helps a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on gabapentin and tramadol for now. The team mentioned possibly weaning tramadol long-term, but that’s not now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d rather avoid opioids, but I need something for the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-09-05 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with you on that. For now, your priority is mental health stabilization."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-09-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lithium level came back at 0.3, which is low. Psychiatry wants to increase your dose to 300 mg at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-09-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? I’ve heard lithium can have side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-09-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll monitor your levels and kidney function. At the right dose, it’s very effective for bipolar disorder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-09-06 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust the team. I just want to feel like myself again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-09-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a heads-up—your port placement is scheduled for tomorrow morning. The radiology team will confirm the placement with a chest X-ray after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-09-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. Will I be asleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-09-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get sedation, so you’ll be very relaxed and won’t feel pain. You might remember bits, but mostly you’ll just sleep through it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-09-07 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds okay. I’m just nervous about recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-09-07 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have some soreness and swelling, but it usually improves in a few days. We’ll keep the site clean and check it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-09-08 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back. The port was placed successfully. The chest X-ray confirms the tip is in the right spot—near your heart where it should be."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-09-08 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. It’s sore, but I can deal with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-09-08 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s some swelling and mild tenderness, which is normal. We’ll keep the dressing on for now and change it tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-09-08 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to use my arm okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-09-08 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, just avoid heavy lifting for a few days. You’ll get instructions on care before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-09-09 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your follow-up labs look good. Hemoglobin improved, electrolytes stable. Lithium level pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-09-09 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ve been feeling a little more present. Still flat, but not as dark."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-09-09 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. The ECT is scheduled for Thursday. Being here helps ensure you’re medically stable for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-09-09 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about ECT, but it’s helped before. I just hate the memory fog."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-09-09 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor you closely. The benefits often outweigh the side effects, especially when mood is severely affected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-09-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Lithium level is back—0.6, which is better. Still a bit low, but moving in the right direction. We’ll keep you on 300 mg nightly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-09-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been sleeping better since the dose went up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-09-10 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Trazodone and the lithium are likely helping. Any nausea or tremors?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-09-10 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-09-10 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your port site is healing well—less swelling, no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-09-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow’s your ECT. After that, you’ll be transferred to Deaconess 4, the psychiatric unit, for continued care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-09-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m ready for the next step. I feel safer here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-09-11 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad to hear that. You’ve made real progress. We’ll keep you on all your current meds, including tramadol for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-09-11 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the lithium stays at 300 mg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-09-11 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for now. The psych team will follow up on levels and adjust if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had ECT this morning—went smoothly. You’re awake, alert, and oriented. No complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a little groggy, but okay. My head doesn’t hurt."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. The grogginess should pass in a few hours. Your port site is healing well—just mild tenderness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’m glad it’s in. Makes things easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re discharging you to Deaconess 4. They’ll continue your psychiatric care, including ECT and medication management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I keep the same meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—gabapentin, omeprazole, tramadol, levothyroxine, trazodone, and lithium 300 mg at night. We’re also adding hydroxyzine for anxiety if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. And my mom will be my contact?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we have her as your contact. You’re alert, walking on your own, and medically stable. We’re confident you’re ready for the transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I feel like I’m on a better path now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve worked hard this week. Keep reaching out when you need help. That’s how we stay ahead of these episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I don’t want to go back to that place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re not alone in this. The team at Deaconess will support you. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2172-09-12 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in before transfer. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "More clear-headed. Still tired from ECT, but okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. You’re doing well. The port is secure, your labs are stable, and your mental status is clear."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go. I feel safer knowing I’ll keep getting treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad. You’ve made real progress. The team at Deaconess will continue your care plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m hopeful this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hope is important. Keep using your tools—meds, therapy, and reaching out. You’ve got this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you doing well soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask. Rest up before transfer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in with discharge instructions and your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good luck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2172-09-12 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-09-04 16:46:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-09-12 19:57:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 34-year-old woman with bipolar disorder and a history of suicide attempts was admitted after reporting suicidal ideation with a plan to drive into a tree. She was stabilized in the ED and admitted for monitoring and psychiatric disposition planning. During her stay, she was started on lithium, which was titrated to 300 mg nightly based on therapeutic levels. A port-a-cath was successfully placed for ongoing ECT treatments due to poor venous access, with post-procedure imaging confirming proper placement. She underwent ECT during the admission and remained medically stable. Her chronic abdominal pain, likely from endometriosis, was managed with gabapentin and tramadol, and other chronic conditions including asthma, GERD, and hypothyroidism were maintained on current regimens. She was discharged to an inpatient psychiatric facility for continued care, alert, interactive, and with a clear mental status.",
    "problems": [
      "Bipolar disorder, current episode depressed, severe, without psychotic features",
      "Hypotension, unspecified",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Chronic pain syndrome"
    ]
  }
}
